    "description": "Assorted collection of 23 vintage and antique sterling silver flatware and serving pieces from several makers and patterns. Marks visible include Gorham Sterling, Skern & Son Sterling, and additional sterling maker marks. The collection includes teaspoons, larger spoons, forks, specialty forks, butter spreaders/knives, serving pieces, and an unusual sterling napkin ring with applied bird decoration.\nSeveral pieces have attractive period designs, and some are monogrammed which appear to be the letter “W” — see second photo for full collection.\nPieces show normal age-related surface scratches, tarnish, and wear consistent with use.\nOf particular interest are the Gorham Willow sterling pieces. Willow was introduced by Gorham in 1954. One teaspoon has damage seen in photo #18.\nTotal weight 1 lb 6 oz. Plus one knife with sterling handle and stainless blade.",
